<title>UK: SBN Bank sets $50 million eight-year step-up FRN.</title>
<headline>SBN Bank sets $50 million eight-year step-up FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SBN BANK</p>
<p> AMT    $50 MLN	 BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY     2004</p>
<p> TYPE  STEP-UP FRN    MARGIN   **75 BP     PAY DATE    16.DEC.96</p>
<p> REOFFER    99.35     ISS PRICE  99.35     FULL FEES   0.5</p>
<p> NOTES    **FOR FIRST FIVE YEARS THEN STEPS-UP TO 225 BP</p>
<p>		CALL IN WHOLE (NOT IN PART) IN YEAR FIVE AND</p>
<p>		THEREAFTER ON INTEREST PAYMENT DATES</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 NEG PLG    NO	  GOV LAW     ENGLISH</p>
<p> TAX PROVS  STANDARD  MGT/UND    0.35	SELL CONC  0.15</p>
<p> NOTES	REOFFER YIELD OF 3M-LIBOR +90 BP.</p>
<p>		UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED. SUBORDINATED</p>
<p>		PROVISIONS SUBJECT TO DANISH LAW.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
